{"id":"sw-4df655","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Foundation \u0026 Toolchain: Rust workspace, wgpu on Metal+Vulkan, first compute raymarch","description":"Stand up the project skeleton and prove the whole toolchain end-to-end before any architecture exists.\n\n**Scope**\n- Rust workspace: `engine` library crate + `viewer` binary crate\n- winit window, wgpu device/surface init — native Metal (macOS) and Vulkan (Win/Linux)\n- Compute-shader raymarcher rendering one dense 256³ brick\n- egui debug overlay, GPU timestamp queries and frame stats from day one\n- CI building all three platforms\n\n**Exit criteria**: the dense brick renders at interactive rates on macOS/Metal and at least one Vulkan target, with live GPU timings on screen. Measurement tooling is non-negotiable — the prior Godot experiment's lessons all came from measuring.","sort_order":"a0","labels":["epic","infra"]},"created_at":"2026-08-05T19:23:30.292177Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-aa609f","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Sparse World \u0026 Core Raymarcher: brick pool, DDA traversal, first generated world","description":"The core data structure and traversal loop. World voxels at **10 cm** base scale, stored as 16³ bricks (1.6 m per brick) in a pooled allocator, addressed by a shallow top-level index.\n\n**Scope**\n- Brick pool allocator; per-brick material palettes (8-bit indices)\n- Top-level index + hierarchical DDA traversal in a compute shader\n- Surface normals, primary shadow ray\n- Volumetric procedural generator v0: 3D density + material function (heightfield + strata + caves), not a heightmap\n\n**Exit criteria**: free-fly around a generated sparse world with sun shadows, entirely raymarched — no meshes anywhere.","sort_order":"a1","labels":["epic","rendering"]},"created_at":"2026-08-05T19:23:30.312707Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-b254c8","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Scene Structure: voxel object instances + two-level TLAS traversal","description":"The world is not one grid: it is a terrain volume plus voxel **object instances** (tree, tower, prop), each owning a local brick tree, a transform, and a per-instance voxel scale (this is the future path to finer-than-10cm props). Load-bearing for destruction (per-object connectivity), dynamic debris rendering, and LOD.\n\n**Scope**\n- Voxel object type: local brick tree + transform + per-instance scale\n- TLAS BVH over instances, refit per frame\n- Two-level ray traversal: TLAS hit → transform ray to object space → same DDA\n\n**Exit criteria**: hundreds of instanced objects rendered by the identical raymarcher code path, movable at runtime.","sort_order":"a2","labels":["epic","rendering"]},"created_at":"2026-08-05T19:23:30.332317Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-d6d2c2","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Streaming \u0026 LOD: SSE-driven traversal, paging, memory budget, DAG compaction","description":"Scale to km horizons under a fixed memory budget. Core policy from notes.md: **never do sub-pixel work** — Screen-Space Error drives traversal termination, so LOD is a traversal-stop rule, crack-free by construction.\n\n**Scope**\n- SSE-driven traversal termination (~1–2 px node footprint)\n- Brick mip chain build + re-filter\n- Async disk→VRAM paging with residency tracking and a hard memory budget\n- Background SVDAG compaction for cold regions (hot/cold model: DAG is a compression cache for immutable data; anything edited un-merges back to bricks)\n\n**Exit criteria**: km-scale world flies hitch-free under budget, GPU timers confirm no sub-pixel traversal.","sort_order":"a3","labels":["epic","rendering","perf"]},"created_at":"2026-08-05T19:23:30.358443Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-d9e5c0","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Editing \u0026 Persistence: CSG ops, copy-on-write bricks, op log","description":"Real-time volumetric editing anywhere in the world — cost bounded by edit volume, never by distance.\n\n**Scope**\n- CSG edit ops (sphere/box subtract and place, material-aware)\n- Copy-on-write un-merge from DAG into mutable bricks (Careil \u0026 Billeter 2020)\n- Upward mip re-filter along edited paths so coarse LODs show the edit\n- Per-region **op log**: persistence = procedural base + compressed DAG + op log; lazy full-res replay when the player approaches a coarsely-edited region\n- Collision proxy refresh for dirty bricks\n\n**Exit criteria**: dig a tunnel at 60 fps; quit and reload; the tunnel persists. Edit a distant structure and see it change at its rendered LOD.","sort_order":"a4","labels":["epic","engine"]},"created_at":"2026-08-05T19:23:30.373288Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-b815a0","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Destruction \u0026 Physics: connectivity, island extraction, rigid voxel bodies","description":"Chop a tree — the top falls. Blow a hole in a castle wall — debris tumbles. Tunnel under a wall — it collapses.\n\n**Scope**\n- Per-brick connectivity summaries + brick adjacency graph (search bricks, not voxels)\n- Async island detection after edits: flood from both sides of the cut; the side that can't reach the object's anchor goes dynamic (runs over 1–3 frames)\n- Island extraction into dynamic voxel bodies; mass/COM/inertia summed exactly from occupancy\n- rapier integration (voxel/compound colliders); no scripted topple — contact with the stump does it\n- Object anchor rules; terrain edits queue re-anchor checks on intersecting objects (undermining works)\n- Settling: sleep at rest, never re-voxelize into the world; coarsen/despawn small debris\n\nTerrain itself is exempt from collapse (Minecraft rule; cave-in support is a deferred design knob).\n\n**Exit criteria**: the three scenarios above work end-to-end, driven by edits, with no per-case scripting.","sort_order":"a5","labels":["epic","physics"]},"created_at":"2026-08-05T19:23:30.387815Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-c13774","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Lighting \u0026 GI: screen-space first, cone-traced voxel mips as world fallback","description":"Lumen's architecture, cheaper on voxels: the voxel mip chain *is* the world-space tracing structure Lumen has to fake with SDFs and surface caches.\n\n**Scope**\n- Cone tracing through voxel mips: sky occlusion + AO\n- One-bounce diffuse GI — screen-space trace first, world-space cone fallback\n- Emissive materials; tonemapping/exposure pipeline\n\n**Exit criteria**: dug tunnels go dark naturally with no light-propagation hack; GI visibly responds to edits (opening a wall lets light in).","sort_order":"a6","labels":["epic","rendering"]},"created_at":"2026-08-05T19:23:30.401478Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-b146f7","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Materials, Digging \u0026 Ore: dig tools, vein generation, collectible mineral chunks","description":"First gameplay-shaped feature set, built entirely from Editing + Destruction machinery — digging is pure edit pipeline (no connectivity), ore collection is material-filtered island extraction.\n\n**Scope**\n- Dig tool: shovel scoop edits + short-lived dirt debris bodies\n- Ore vein generation in the volumetric generator (material noise)\n- Material-filtered extraction: mined voxels *become* the collectible chunk body, rendered by the same raymarcher\n- Pickup + minimal inventory hook (chunk voxel data doubles as item model/icon)\n\n**Exit criteria**: find a vein, mine it, the chunk drops, pick it up, it's in inventory after reload.","sort_order":"a7","labels":["epic","gameplay"]},"created_at":"2026-08-05T19:23:30.417044Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-3a604e","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Write technical design document (docs/DESIGN.md)","description":"Capture the architecture decided in design discussion (2026-08-05) as `docs/DESIGN.md`: goals, stack decision (Rust + wgpu), 10 cm voxel scale, hybrid brick-pool/SVDAG data model, object-instance scene structure, editing/op-log persistence, destruction pipeline, GI approach, milestone ladder, risks.","status":"PLANNED","parent_id":"sw-4df655","estimate":2,"sort_order":"a0","labels":["docs"]},"created_at":"2026-08-05T19:23:54.326227Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-10ef86","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Scaffold Rust workspace: engine + viewer crates, CI for macOS/Windows/Linux","description":"Cargo workspace with `engine` (library) and `viewer` (binary). CI builds + clippy + fmt on all three platforms. Establish shader directory layout (WGSL) and asset path conventions.","parent_id":"sw-4df655","estimate":2,"sort_order":"a8","labels":["feature","infra"]},"created_at":"2026-08-05T19:23:56.27138Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-a2446a","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"winit window + wgpu device/surface init with egui debug overlay","description":"Window, swapchain, resize handling, free-fly camera input. egui overlay for live debug values. Verify Metal backend on macOS explicitly (adapter info surfaced in overlay).","parent_id":"sw-4df655","estimate":2,"sort_order":"a9","labels":["feature","infra"]},"created_at":"2026-08-05T19:23:58.688358Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-ce3a9f","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Compute-shader raymarcher: one dense 256³ brick","description":"Fullscreen compute pass raymarching a dense 256³ voxel volume in a storage buffer. Proves the whole toolchain (WGSL, bind groups, storage buffers, present) before any sparse structure exists. Toolchain spike — throwaway traversal code is fine.","parent_id":"sw-4df655","estimate":3,"sort_order":"aA","labels":["feature","rendering"]},"created_at":"2026-08-05T19:24:01.018112Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-c96adf","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"GPU timestamp queries + frame stats overlay","description":"wgpu timestamp queries around each pass, rolling averages in the egui overlay. Measurement discipline from day one — every perf lesson in notes.md came from measuring, not guessing.","parent_id":"sw-4df655","estimate":2,"sort_order":"aB","labels":["feature","perf"]},"created_at":"2026-08-05T19:24:03.32905Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-3afd48","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Brick pool allocator: 16³ bricks with per-brick material palettes","description":"Pooled GPU allocator for 16³ bricks (1.6 m at 10 cm voxels). Voxel = 8-bit palette index into a per-brick material palette. Free-list recycling; stable brick handles for the index to reference.","parent_id":"sw-aa609f","estimate":3,"sort_order":"aC","labels":["feature","engine"]},"created_at":"2026-08-05T19:24:05.770422Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-30aa3c","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Top-level brick index + DDA traversal compute shader","description":"Shallow top-level index (grid or shallow tree) mapping world space → brick handles. Hierarchical DDA: coarse steps through empty space, descend into bricks, per-voxel DDA inside. Empty-space skipping is the core perf primitive.","parent_id":"sw-aa609f","estimate":5,"sort_order":"aD","labels":["feature","rendering"]},"created_at":"2026-08-05T19:24:08.035375Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-15accc","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Surface normals + primary shadow ray","description":"Face normals from DDA hit axis (voxel look) plus optional smoothed variant from occupancy gradient. One sun shadow ray per hit through the same traversal.","parent_id":"sw-aa609f","estimate":3,"sort_order":"aE","labels":["feature","rendering"]},"created_at":"2026-08-05T19:24:10.385883Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-00ae86","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Volumetric generator v0: 3D density/material function (heightfield, strata, caves)","description":"Generator is a 3D density + material function, not a heightmap — underground must contain strata and caves so digging (sw-b146f7) has something to find. Deterministic from seed; generates bricks on demand.","parent_id":"sw-aa609f","estimate":5,"sort_order":"aF","labels":["feature","worldgen"]},"created_at":"2026-08-05T19:24:12.28516Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-5d894d","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Voxel object type: local brick tree + transform + per-instance scale","description":"Objects (tree, tower, prop) own a local brick grid/tree, a rigid transform, and a voxel scale — per-instance scale is the upgrade path to finer-than-10cm props. Terrain remains a special identity-transform volume.","parent_id":"sw-b254c8","estimate":3,"sort_order":"aG","labels":["feature","engine"]},"created_at":"2026-08-05T19:24:14.887632Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-b975c9","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"TLAS BVH over object instances with per-frame refit","description":"Small BVH over instance AABBs, refit each frame (rebuild on structural change). Uploaded alongside instance table (transform, inverse, scale, root pointer).","parent_id":"sw-b254c8","estimate":3,"sort_order":"aH","labels":["feature","rendering"]},"created_at":"2026-08-05T19:24:17.00404Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-06bbbc","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Two-level traversal: TLAS hit → object-local DDA","description":"Rays test the TLAS, transform into object space, and run the identical brick DDA. One code path renders terrain, placed objects, and (later) falling debris. Closest-hit across terrain + instances.","parent_id":"sw-b254c8","estimate":5,"sort_order":"aI","labels":["feature","rendering"]},"created_at":"2026-08-05T19:24:18.861391Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-1b7156","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"SSE-driven traversal termination (no sub-pixel work)","description":"Stop descending when a node's projected footprint falls below ~1–2 px and shade from the mip. This is the notes.md conclusion #1 (\"never submit sub-pixel geometry\") expressed as a traversal rule — crack-free by construction, no skirts, no seams.","parent_id":"sw-d6d2c2","estimate":3,"sort_order":"aJ","labels":["feature","rendering","perf"]},"created_at":"2026-08-05T19:24:21.299337Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-638630","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Brick mip chain build + re-filter","description":"Downsampled occupancy + averaged material/color per brick level, built at generation and re-filtered on change. Consumed by SSE termination (near/far shading) and later by cone-traced GI (sw-c13774).","parent_id":"sw-d6d2c2","estimate":3,"sort_order":"aK","labels":["feature","rendering"]},"created_at":"2026-08-05T19:24:23.663948Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-943a75","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Async disk→VRAM paging with residency tracking + memory budget","description":"Multithreaded generate/load → upload pipeline keyed by camera + SSE demand. Hard VRAM budget with LRU eviction of cold bricks (coarse mips stay resident). The riskiest single story in the ladder; hitch-free flight is the bar.","parent_id":"sw-d6d2c2","estimate":8,"sort_order":"aL","labels":["feature","engine","perf"]},"created_at":"2026-08-05T19:24:26.422271Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-295087","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Background SVDAG compaction for cold regions","description":"Deduplicate quiet regions into a DAG (70–90% memory reduction per notes.md); traversal reads DAG nodes transparently. Hot/cold contract: any edit un-merges the affected subtree back into pool bricks (sw-d9e5c0). Deliberately late in the ladder — bricks alone carry the world until budgets demand this.","parent_id":"sw-d6d2c2","estimate":8,"sort_order":"aM","labels":["feature","engine"]},"created_at":"2026-08-05T19:24:29.18484Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-6e6251","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"CSG edit ops: sphere/box subtract \u0026 place through copy-on-write bricks","description":"Material-aware subtract/place brushes. Edits anywhere: if the target subtree is DAG-compressed, un-merge just the root-to-leaf paths (O(depth) new nodes) into pool bricks, apply, mark hot. Cost bounded by edit volume, never by distance. Removed-voxel data is capturable by callers (feeds extraction in sw-b815a0/sw-b146f7).","parent_id":"sw-d9e5c0","estimate":5,"sort_order":"aN","labels":["feature","engine"]},"created_at":"2026-08-05T19:24:36.346832Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-97fed0","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Edit-triggered upward mip re-filter","description":"Re-filter the parent chain of every edited brick so distant/coarse LOD views show the hole. Without this, edits exist in data but not on screen for far objects. O(depth) per changed brick, background thread.","parent_id":"sw-d9e5c0","estimate":2,"sort_order":"aO","labels":["feature","rendering"]},"created_at":"2026-08-05T19:24:38.711879Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-5b1f5e","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Per-region op log: persistence + lazy full-res replay","description":"World = procedural base + compressed DAG + ordered edit-op log per region. Distant edits apply immediately at resident LODs; full-res replay deferred until the player approaches. Save files proportional to what players changed. Save/load round-trip is the acceptance test.","parent_id":"sw-d9e5c0","estimate":5,"sort_order":"aP","labels":["feature","engine"]},"created_at":"2026-08-05T19:24:41.074985Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-dcdb8e","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Collision proxy refresh for dirty bricks","description":"Character/body collision derived from voxel data must update when bricks change — the player stands in the hole they just dug. Rebuild on the same background thread as mip re-filter.","parent_id":"sw-d9e5c0","estimate":3,"sort_order":"aQ","labels":["feature","physics"]},"created_at":"2026-08-05T19:24:43.431628Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-b3790f","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Per-brick connectivity summaries + brick adjacency graph","description":"Per brick: which of its faces connect through solid voxels internally. Connectivity questions then run on the brick graph (thousands of nodes) instead of voxels (millions), descending to voxel level only inside bricks the cut touched. Summaries recomputed only for dirty bricks.","parent_id":"sw-b815a0","estimate":3,"sort_order":"aR","labels":["feature","physics"]},"created_at":"2026-08-05T19:24:45.362035Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-305917","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Async island detection: two-sided flood fill to anchor","description":"After an edit to an object, flood from both sides of the cut on the brick graph; the side that cannot reach the object's anchor becomes a detached island. Budgeted, async over 1–3 frames (30–50 ms latency imperceptible). Per-object scope keeps worst case bounded.","parent_id":"sw-b815a0","estimate":5,"sort_order":"aS","labels":["feature","physics"]},"created_at":"2026-08-05T19:24:48.131544Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-f5b640","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Island extraction into dynamic voxel bodies (mass/COM/inertia from occupancy)","description":"Copy detached voxels into a new object instance (own brick grid + origin), subtract from source via the standard edit op. Mass, center of mass, inertia tensor are exact sums over occupancy × material density. Rendered by the existing two-level traversal — no special case.","parent_id":"sw-b815a0","estimate":5,"sort_order":"aT","labels":["feature","physics"]},"created_at":"2026-08-05T19:24:50.611186Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-d6b1da","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"rapier integration: colliders for dynamic voxel bodies","description":"rapier3d rigid bodies for extracted islands. Prefer rapier's voxel colliders if current; fallback is greedy-merged box compounds from coarse mips. No scripted topple — contact between falling top and stump produces the tip-and-slide naturally. Verify rapier voxel-collider status at implementation time.","parent_id":"sw-b815a0","estimate":5,"sort_order":"aU","labels":["feature","physics"]},"created_at":"2026-08-05T19:24:52.841586Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-585309","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Object anchor rules + re-anchor checks on terrain edits","description":"Anchor = object base bricks contacting solid terrain. Terrain edits that dirty bricks intersecting an object's anchor region queue a re-anchor check on that object — tunneling under the castle wall brings it down through the standard pipeline. Undermining as emergent behavior, not a scripted feature.","parent_id":"sw-b815a0","estimate":3,"sort_order":"aV","labels":["feature","physics"]},"created_at":"2026-08-05T19:24:55.217245Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-0bfac1","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Debris settling: sleep, coarsen, despawn policy","description":"Bodies at rest sleep as instances — never re-voxelized into the world (rotated grids resample lossily). Small debris coarsens/despawns over time to bound instance count.","parent_id":"sw-b815a0","estimate":2,"sort_order":"aW","labels":["feature","physics"]},"created_at":"2026-08-05T19:24:57.565478Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-e1c578","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Cone tracing through voxel mips: AO + sky occlusion","description":"Cones through the brick mip chain for ambient occlusion and sky visibility. First proof that the mip chain doubles as the GI tracing structure — tunnels go dark with zero light-propagation code.","parent_id":"sw-c13774","estimate":5,"sort_order":"aX","labels":["feature","rendering"]},"created_at":"2026-08-05T19:24:59.910286Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-d3ae86","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"One-bounce diffuse GI: screen-space trace first, world-space cone fallback","description":"Lumen's hybrid architecture on voxel-native structures: screen-space ray trace for detail, cone trace through mips when rays leave the screen. Temporal accumulation for stability. GI must respond to edits (opening a wall lets light in) since it traces live data.","parent_id":"sw-c13774","estimate":8,"sort_order":"aY","labels":["feature","rendering"]},"created_at":"2026-08-05T19:25:02.246008Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-ac8f44","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Emissive materials + tonemapping/exposure pipeline","description":"Emissive as a material property (glowing ore, lava, torches) picked up by both GI paths. HDR accumulation, filmic tonemap, auto-exposure for cave↔surface transitions.","parent_id":"sw-c13774","estimate":3,"sort_order":"aZ","labels":["feature","rendering"]},"created_at":"2026-08-05T19:25:04.132274Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-1a041a","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Dig tool: shovel scoop edits + dirt debris","description":"Player-facing digging: aimed scoop subtract with material-dependent rates, short-lived dirt-clod debris bodies for feedback. Pure edit-pipeline consumer — no connectivity checks (terrain exempt from collapse).","parent_id":"sw-b146f7","estimate":3,"sort_order":"aa","labels":["feature","gameplay"]},"created_at":"2026-08-05T19:25:06.973075Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-14b47c","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Ore vein generation: material noise in the volumetric generator","description":"Vein-shaped material noise (e.g. ridged/worm noise) assigning ore material IDs within stone strata, depth-dependent distribution per ore type.","parent_id":"sw-b146f7","estimate":3,"sort_order":"ab","labels":["feature","worldgen"]},"created_at":"2026-08-05T19:25:08.849467Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-985dc7","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Material-filtered extraction: mined voxels become collectible chunk bodies","description":"Breaking a vein captures the removed ore voxels (island-extraction machinery, driven by the edit's material filter instead of flood fill) into a small dynamic body — the chunk you pick up is literally the voxels you mined.","parent_id":"sw-b146f7","estimate":3,"sort_order":"ac","labels":["feature","gameplay"]},"created_at":"2026-08-05T19:25:11.263555Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-4f3a27","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Pickup + minimal inventory hook","description":"Proximity pickup despawns the chunk instance and records an inventory entry; chunk voxel data retained as item model/icon. Deliberately minimal — full inventory UI belongs to the future game layer.","parent_id":"sw-b146f7","estimate":2,"sort_order":"ad","labels":["feature","gameplay"]},"created_at":"2026-08-05T19:25:13.075522Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
